The numbers is a list of 1, 2, 3, and 5, while the rank is 3.
The numerators is an empty list of whole numbers.
The denominators is an empty list of whole numbers.
For every left from 0 to 3.
For every right from left plus 1 to 3.
Place item left of numbers into numerators.
Place item right of numbers into denominators.

The count is the number of items in numerators.
The final is count minus 1.
For every pass from 0 to final.
For every spot from 0 to count minus 2.
The next is spot plus 1.
The lowproduct is item spot of numerators times item next of denominators.
The highproduct is item next of numerators times item spot of denominators.
If lowproduct is more than highproduct, swap item spot of numerators and item next of numerators, swap item spot of denominators and item next of denominators.

The chosen is rank minus 1.
Show item chosen of numerators.
Show item chosen of denominators.
